 ## Diagnosis record
 
 - Confirmed: current snapshot item naming fails on NBT-wrapped modern custom text; native `!inventory` returns only counts and armor IDs.
 - Confirmed: replaying the real crowded inventory at 400 tokens produces `inventory={details:'minecraft_observe'}`; at 700 tokens it keeps only the first sixteen counts and drops named-item identity.
-- To verify: failure history/decision grounding and actual command availability at the native prompt boundary.
+- Confirmed: the executor exposes `!goToSurface`, `!pillarUp`, `!craftRecipe`, `!serverQuery` and `!serverCommand`; none are blocked in this deployment. The local profile duplicated its Chinese execution policy and contained literal newline escapes in its protocol template.
+- Confirmed: terminal callbacks can run before passive state and previously contained up to 12,500 feedback characters without current resource facts. Matched outcome history and bounded fresh state now accompany priority decisions.
+- Confirmed during live verification: `plugin/server/messaging/proactive_bridge.py` calls the generic result-summary parser before the documented callback cap. A real 840-token idle decision became 200 tokens and lost `resources`; the actual conversation bus confirmed the loss. This platform-layer change requires escalation under `CONTEXT.md`.
+- Prepared and verified a scoped host patch that preserves Minecraft v2 text up to the existing 1,000-token callback cap. Other plugin/legacy paths retain their 200-token parsing behavior. Application is pending the user's response to the escalation question; no platform source was modified.
+
+## Verification and deployment record (2026-10-09)
+
+- Native working suite: 238 tests passed; contribution checkout: 244 tests passed.
+- Complete Minecraft plugin suite: 98 tests passed, including modern text identity, crowded budgets, matched history, stale/foreign results and timeout recovery.
+- Export/deployment source commits: native `eb7ba40`, `8420406`; Neko plugin `369532f`, `a8e28a5`, `c6a64d8`.
+- Reloaded the Minecraft body and its plugin with the established lifecycle scripts, retaining the running local model and Neko main. Runtime state/arbitration was preserved.
+- Fresh live observations correctly show the wand, compass and book labels and 8 received/pushed welcome parts. The bot was already on the surface before this deployment; do not attribute that earlier escape to these changes.
+- Read-only sampling observed a genuine autonomous task, inventory changes and later position changes, with no injected diagnostic actions/chat. That task still attempted a long tree-growing chain and ended at its deadline. This is evidence that dispatch works, not evidence of reliable unattended survival.
+- Remaining blocker: the host's earlier 200-token truncation prevents the new bounded context from consistently reaching the model. The companion host patch is reviewable but must not be described as applied until escalation is approved and live delivery is verified.
